WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.767
-Dane, welcome back. Ooh, la la.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:03.901
Dane Cook is here.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.467
-Let me tell you something
about this crowd.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:09.067
Who needs a tree outside being
lit when this crowd's on fire?!

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, wow!

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.501
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.968
That's exactly right.

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.033
-Sit. Please sit.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.467
-They're not standing.
-Sit down.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.667
-They're not standing.
-I need everyone to please sit.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.367
-They're not standing.
They're not standing.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.000
Dane.
-It looks like they're standing.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.767
-Dane, welcome back.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.100
It is the holiday season.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.634
Are you in the holiday spirit,
bud?

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:32.567
-Listen, as you can probably
tell, a festival of lights,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.000
delights, and out of sights is
coursing through by veins.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.667
And I'm just feeling -- I'm
feeling like this is going to be

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.901
a really special time for you,
me, and all of us.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:41.968
What do you think?
-Wow.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.334
-Roots?
-You feeling the Roots too?

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.567
Dane, we've known each other --
we've known each other --

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.501
we've known each other
for a long time.

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:52.934
-Very long time.
-Did I get too close there?

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:54.267
-No, but I like that
we just got intimate.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:55.334
You guys want to step out?

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.300
[ Laughter ]
-We got real intimate.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.300
-You laughed really loud in
my ear and that scared me.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.267
-I apologize. I was too close.
Normally I'm here.

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:03.834
-Jimmy Fallon and I,
we've known each other.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:04.901
We've been on the road.
We've crossed paths.

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.501
-Probably 20 years?

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:09.400
25 years?
-Listen. How about this guy?

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.167
How about the success that Jimmy
Fallon has created for himself?

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:15.033
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-This entire organization.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.868
It's not about me.
It's not about me!

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.200
-Tonight is about Dane Cook.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.567
-It is?
-Yeah.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.100
Dude, you're the greatest.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.167
I had to follow you many a time
at the Improv.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.434
-I made it tough on you,
didn't I?

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.067
-You really were, yeah.
It was great.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.901
And I loved it.
But then to watch you rise

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:31.467
and then you do Madison Square
Garden, I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:32.834
And then, here we are.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.400
We're on "The Tonight Show,"
we're talking again.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.767
We're 50.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.234
-I'm 50 years old,
doing what I love, 31 years in.

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:39.868
-You look great.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.167
You look great, bud.
-I feel great.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.767
-What's it like?
What's it like being 50?

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.868
-Okay, so -- can I just --
can we do this together?

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.634
I'm going to say this,
and on the count of three --

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:52.601
There's one gift at 50 that
everybody wants to, should,

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:54.634
and does ultimately gift
to themselves.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.801
And we can all say it
at the same time. Ready?

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:59.834
And I'll say it, but the
ultimate gift at 50.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.367
Ready? Here we go.
All together. Ready?

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.367
One, two, three.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.133
A colonoscopy!

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.634
-Yes.
-[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.801
-A colonoscopy.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.634
-Yes, we all said it
at the same time.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.834
-That's the butt stuff
that's not so fun.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:19.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:20.467
-Oh, my.
I never heard it that way.

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:21.801
-They made me drink the --

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.801
So, here's what happens
if you've never done it.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.467
You have to drink a liquid

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:26.934
that's basically
like a laxative.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.701
It's called like MiraLAX.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.601
I'm endorsed by them as well.
So thank you to --

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.701
-[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Congratulations.

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:34.300
-So, they gave me a choice.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.868
They said,
"You can do the liquid

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:37.367
or you can do the pill form."

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:40.133
But I was so nervous about
the entire situation,

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.968
I messed up and I did both.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:48.234
And -- Ah.
-Wow.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:54.701
-What happened to my stomach
was something cataclysmic.

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:56.667
-[ Laughter ]
-That's a good word.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:57.901
-It's almost like --
It's a good word.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:00.234
-It is.
-It was almost like --

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:02.400
The way my stomach reacted --

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.234
Okay, first of all, I went
into the bathroom and --

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:07.634
-Never came out.
-[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.434
-Okay. Well, have you ever sat

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:10.934
on the edge of a toilet
like this?

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:15.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.801
Right?
Like you're about to play chess

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.534
with Bobby Fischer
and you know --

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.701
I don't want to be graphic,
but I almost felt like

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.834
this is what a Super Soaker
must feel like.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:31.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:34.167
Too much? Am I cancelled?
Am I cancelled?!

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:37.267
-No, no, no, no.
You're not cancelled.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:39.634
Oh, my God.
But it all went well?

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.334
-Yeah, yeah.
But here's the best part.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.701
I've never done this before. I'm
going to look at this camera.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:46.100
When I walked out of the
bathroom, I remember I took

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.267
three steps and I turned back
and I went,

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:50.100
"We don't talk about this
ever again."

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.968
-Wow, you said that
to the bathroom.

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:53.901
-Yeah.
-And here you are now.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:55.901
Let's talk about "Above It All,"
by the way.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.167
It went to number one on iTunes,
by the way.

00:03:58.167 --> 00:03:59.901
Another number-one album
for you.

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.834
-It's amazing.
-Come on, buddy.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.067
-It's amazing.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:06.467
-But, dude, you've done
Madison Square Garden.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.000
You've done the arenas.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.033
-Yeah, I've done laundromats
outside of Boston.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.234
-Yeah, when you first started.

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:12.834
But now, this one, this special

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:15.400
you did, you did it on the porch
in the front of your house.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.100
-Yeah, I did it on my front
porch in the beautiful

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.968
Hollywood Hills overlooking
that exceptional view.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:23.567
And I brought a bunch of people
to my home who didn't know

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:27.167
they were being shuttled to
my house for my comedy special.

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:29.000
-How did you come up
with the idea?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.567
-I'm a genius.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.334
-[ Laughter ]
-I know that.

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:35.167
-It's the way my brain just --
-But how did you make it work

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:37.033
having all those strangers
at your house?

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:39.767
-Yeah, okay, so, when I was
12 years old, I used to stand on

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.267
the porch and I would do like --

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.901
you know, entertain
the neighbors.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.834
You know how like everybody
would get together on one stoop,

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.400
people would have
a few too many drinks.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.000
There'd be a couple little
weird arguments.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.467
And then somebody would be
a cutup

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.300
and try to make
the neighborhood laugh.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.834
And that's what I did.
And every single year of

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:56.133
my 31 years doing stand-up
comedy, I was always like,

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:59.000
"That would feel like
the ultimate show."

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.400
Because not only is it
big and bombastic,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.367
but it's the most personal
and intimate

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:04.367
because you're in my home
with me.

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:05.767
So I hope you enjoy it

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.300
and have a lot of laughs with me
with "Above It All."

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.567
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:10.501
Here's Dane Cook in his special
"Above It All."

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:11.767
Take a look.

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.400
-I get weird about weddings.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.667
There's something about
weddings.

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:16.200
First of all, I don't do a lot
of impersonations.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.000
Can I do a very quick one
of all of you?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.033
I can do all of you at once.
Ready?

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:23.334
This is anybody here getting a
wedding invitation in the mail.

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:25.100
Ready? [Bleep]

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:30.968
When is it?

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:32.601
You didn't even look at who.
When? When?

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.667
What weekend have you stolen
from me?!

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:35.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:36.701
July 3rd!

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.801
That's great. July 3rd.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.734
Where is it?
Yosemite National Park.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.601
Outside wedding, July 3rd.

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:44.367
That's not going to be
hot as balls.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:47.234
Then you don't even know
who's getting married

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:48.667
'cause I don't speak
calligraphy.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.200
What the [bleep]?
Is that a K, a Q?

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.901
-Yeah, I don't speak
calligraphy.

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:54.434
Dane Cook, everybody!

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:58.634
"Above It All" is available
right now on danecook.com.

